Quick overview
- Use a dedicated calendar for birthdays/milestones (separate from work/calendar clutter).
- Add each event as a recurring yearly event and attach notes (gift ideas, links, mailing address).
- Use multiple reminders (weeks → days → day-of) so you have time to buy/ship/prepare.
- Sync with your phone and share with family if useful.
- Keep a companion list (Notion / Google Sheet / Notes app) with details you’ll want later.

Step‑by‑step (Google Calendar — similar steps work in Apple/Outlook)
1. Create a calendar
   - Open Google Calendar → left column → “+” next to “Other calendars” → “Create new calendar”.
   - Name it “Friends & Family — Birthdays” (color it so it stands out).

2. Add a recurring birthday/milestone
   - Click a date → “More options”.
   - Title: “Jasper (David & [Partner]) — born Apr 2023” (or “David — birthday”).
   - Set “Does not repeat” → choose “Custom” → Repeat yearly.
   - In the Description field add: gift ideas, sizes, addresses, links to wishlists, notes from last year.
   - Add location or contact email if you’ll send a card.
   - Notifications: Add multiple notifications (see sample schedule below).
   - Save to your “Friends & Family — Birthdays” calendar.

3. Link to Contacts for quick access
   - In your Contacts app add people’s birthdays and notes (phone, postal address, gift ideas).
   - Many calendars import birthdays automatically from Contacts.

4. Set reminder schedule (example)
   - 30 days before → “Buy/choose gift” (email + popup)
   - 14 days before → “Order online / check shipping”
   - 3 days before → “Wrap gift / buy card”
   - 1 day before → “Ship gift / finalize card”
   - Day of → “Wish / post message / call”
   - Add reminders as both popup (phone) and email for reliability.

Automation & imports
- Facebook → Export birthdays (if needed) and import to calendar or add to Contacts.
- Use IFTTT/Zapier to create calendar entries from spreadsheets, or to remind you in Slack/phone.
- For frequent card/gift purchases, connect a shopping list app (Todoist, Reminders) with a recurring task.

Companion system (recommended)
- Notion / Google Sheet / Evernote or a physical “Reading Journal” style:
  - Columns: Name | DOB | Relationship | Address | Gift ideas | Favorite things | Last gift given | Notes
  - Add a “Milestones” tab: graduations, anniversaries, baby firsts (with target reminder dates)

Physical backup
- A nice printed wall calendar (or planner) where you write the big dates in one glance.
- Keep a small index card or journal for notes you want to jot down in person.

